 "result_text": "I fixed it in `get_keys` in `sshtunnel.py`: it now searches `DEFAULT_SSH_DIRECTORY` when `host_pkey_directories` is `None` or empty. I haven't run the tests or tried it against real keys, only confirmed the module still imports.\n\nThe cause was the `if host_pkey_directories is not None:` guard around the key search. With the default of `None`, the whole block was skipped, so the `or [DEFAULT_SSH_DIRECTORY]` fallback inside it never ran. I removed the guard and dedented the block.\n\nBecause the guard is gone, `get_keys` now always looks in `~/.ssh` (or `~/ssh` on Windows) unless you pass directories. Nothing can turn that default search off any more, which matches the existing comment on the `host_pkey_directories=None` argument (\"look for keys in ~/.ssh\").",
